# Citation metadata (Citation File Format 1.2.0). The export to the public
# repository sets `version` and `date-released` to each exported tag's; keep
# them at the current version here (part of a version's documentation check).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Presk, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Presk: a compiler for neural networks with exact real semantics"
abstract: >-
  Presk is a domain-specific language for describing, training and running
  neural networks whose programs denote functions over tensors of real
  numbers, with no machine number type, and a compiler that chooses the
  machine types and the order of operations under a declared error budget,
  checked by measurement against an exact reference.
authors:
  - family-names: Silber
    given-names: Georges-André
    affiliation: "Mines Paris – PSL"
    email: georges-andre.silber@minesparis.psl.eu
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-09-19
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/presk-lang/presk"
url: "https://presk-lang.org"
keywords:
  - neural networks
  - domain-specific language
  - compiler
  - floating-point precision
  - error budget
  - exact arithmetic
  - mixed precision
